{"text": "Shelter.\n\n\"Don't move,\" said Jonas. \"Rule three. If the fog comes, stop and stay together.\"\n\n\"But we aren't with the class,\" said Paloma. \"We have to find them!\"\n\nShe walked quickly into the fog. Jonas ran after her. Then he fell between two rocks.\n\n\"Oh! My leg!\"\n\nPaloma ran back. Jonas sat on the wet ground and held his leg. His face was white.\n\n\"Can you stand?\"\n\nHe tried, but he sat down again. \"I can't walk on it. I'm sorry.\"\n\n\"No, I'm sorry,\" said Paloma. \"This is because of me. Me and my flower.\"\n\nPaloma took out her phone. It did not work up here.\n\n\"Mrs Berg is going to look for us,\" said Jonas. \"So we should stay in one place.\"\n\nThe wind was cold, and the fog was wet. Their clothes were wet, too.\n\n\"We must keep warm,\" said Jonas. \"My dad says that's the most important thing.\"\n\nNear the flower, there was a big rock. Slowly, they moved behind it, away from the wind.\n\nPaloma had her orange jacket, a hat and some chocolate. Jonas had a thin silver blanket in his bag.\n\n\"Mrs Berg gave everybody one this morning,\" he said. \"Didn't you listen?\"\n\n\"I was taking photos,\" said Paloma.\n\nThey put the silver blanket around them both. It was warmer. They ate half of the chocolate and kept the other half.\n\n\"Tell me something,\" said Paloma. \"Something boring. Then I can forget the fog.\"\n\nSo Jonas told her about his little sister and her three fish. The fish were called One, Two and Three. They were very boring fish.\n\nPaloma laughed. Time passed slowly.\n\nAt five o'clock, the fog was darker.\n\n\"It's going to be dark at seven,\" said Jonas. \"We can't stay here all night.\"\n\nThen they heard the bells again. They were closer now.\n\n\"What is it?\" asked Paloma quietly.\n\n\"I don't know.\" Jonas looked tired. His leg was bigger now.\n\nPaloma tried to remember Mrs Berg's rules. Rule one: stay on the path. Rule two: stay with a friend. Rule three: stop in the fog.\n\nAnd rule four? She remembered a blue butterfly and a click. Nothing more.\n\n\"Jonas, what was rule four?\"\n\nJonas closed his eyes. \"Something about listening? I can't think. My leg hurts too much.\"\n\nThen something moved in the fog. It was a big, dark shape. Then there was another one. And another one.\n\nThe shapes were coming towards them.", "textSha256": "e1963a7f3ba3d2a2b42771a8580f8ace9b672e95d6401ed1cf91f1e4c2bbb9b5", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.95, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "alignment": {"characters": ["S", "h", "e", "l", "t", "e", "r", ".", "\n", "\n", "\"", "D", "o", "n", "'", "t", " ", "m", "o", "v", "e", ",", "\"", " ", "s", "a", "i", "d", " ", "J", "o", "n", "a", "s", ".", " ", "\"", "R", "u", "l", "e", " ", "t", "h", "r", "e", "e", ".", " ", "I", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "o", "g", " ", "c", "o", "m", "e", "s", ",", " ", "s", "t", "o", "p", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "s", "t", "a", "y", " ", "t", "o", "g", "e", "t", "h", "e", "r", ".", "\"", "\n", "\n", "\"", "B", "u", "t", " ", "w", "e", " ", "a", "r", "e", "n", "'", "t", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "l", "a", "s", "s", ",", "\"", " ", "s", "a", "i", "d", " ", "P", "a", "l", "o", "m", "a", ".", " ", "\"", "W", "e", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "t", "o", " ", "f", "i", "n", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", "m", "!", "\"", "\n", "\n", "S", "h", "e", " ", "w", "a", "l", "k", "e", "d", " ", "q", "u", "i", "c", "k", "l", "y", " ", "i", "n", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "o", "g", ".", " ", "J", "o", "n", "a", "s", " ", "r", "a", "n", " ", "a", "f", "t", "e", "r", " ", "h", "e", "r", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", "n", " ", "h", "e", " ", "f", "e", "l", "l", " ", "b", "e", "t", "w", "e", "e", "n", " ", "t", "w", "o", " ", "r", "o", "c", "k", "s", ".", "\n", "\n", "\"", "O", "h", "!", " ", "M", "y", " ", "l", "e", "g", "!", "\"", "\n", "\n", "P", "a", "l", "o", "m", "a", " ", "r", "a", "n", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", ".", " ", "J", "o", "n", "a", "s", " "